WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.120
You'd be forgiven for forgetting about&nbsp;
Passengers, but Jennifer Lawrence never will.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:11.040
If you can't recall, Passengers is a sci-fi movie&nbsp;
focusing on Lawrence and Chris Pratt's characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.960
Aurora Lane and Jim Preston. They are two&nbsp;
passengers among many on an interstellar journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.920
and Aurora and Jim wake up early - 90&nbsp;
years too early, as a matter of fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.880
with no obvious way to go back to sleep.&nbsp;
When you have 90 years to kill with someone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.840
things are likely to turn romantic out of&nbsp;
sheer boredom, if nothing else. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.520
even though Lawrence and Pratt&nbsp;
have strong on-screen chemistry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:41.280
the act of filming those steamy scenes was&nbsp;
decidedly flaccid, especially for Lawrence.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.760
The actress recently opened up about&nbsp;
the many ways in which her experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.280
getting intimate with her co-star&nbsp;
was less than ideal — through no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.240
real fault of Pratt's. That doesn't mean&nbsp;
she despised filming Passengers. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.120
whenever she had to get all lovey-dovey in&nbsp;
the film, things turned awkward quickly.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.880
During a roundtable discussion&nbsp;
hosted by The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.080
Jennifer Lawrence revealed&nbsp;
that Passengers had her first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.040
intimate scene ever on film and she used&nbsp;
liquid courage to help her get through.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.920
Lawrence said she felt extremely awkward&nbsp;
knowing the scenes she had to film. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:22.640
to prepare for her big moment, she drank. A lot.&nbsp;
All that alcohol had unintended consequences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.080
though. Lawrence grappled with extreme anxiety&nbsp;
in between shoots. While Lawrence knew her job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.200
was to kiss the then-married-to-Anna Faris&nbsp;
Chris Pratt, even the feigned infidelity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.080
gave her a queasy feeling every time the two&nbsp;
had to lock lips in front of the cameras.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:43.440
To make matters worse, the actual process of&nbsp;
filming romantic scenes was less than fun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.480
One scene that was cut from the film required&nbsp;
Pratt and Lawrence to rock a table back and forth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.240
and neither of them liked it. When&nbsp;
asked about the scene, Lawrence said:

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.360
"Sex scenes are the most&nbsp;
unsexy things in the world."

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:04.000
"I can't think of anything else to try to save us,&nbsp;
and I don't even want to think about it anymore."

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.880
The duo's onscreen romance also led to some real&nbsp;
world problems. When acting in a romantic movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.760
there is always the unspoken fear that&nbsp;
fiction will bleed over into reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.960
complicating real-life relationships. When&nbsp;
two stars have blazing on-screen chemistry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.200
it's a law of the universe that the rumor mill&nbsp;
is going to kick into overdrive. Just ask Bradley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.560
Cooper and Lady Gaga. While many celebrities&nbsp;
understand that this is part of the job and can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.880
find the mental fortitude to rise above it, this&nbsp;
gossip almost always takes a psychological toll.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.720
Tales of behind-the-scenes infidelity spread&nbsp;
like wildfire after Chris Pratt and his wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.920
actress Anna Faris, announced their divorce.&nbsp;
Jennifer Lawrence was at the top of the list&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:56.000
of potential causes, due unfairly to the romantic&nbsp;
scenes she filmed with Pratt during Passengers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.640
Lawrence shot those rumors down during an&nbsp;
interview with InStyle, stating that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.920
film had already been wrapped for years by the&nbsp;
time Faris and Pratt announced their divorce.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.560
Not even Anna Faris bought into the&nbsp;
rumors. In her memoir Unqualified,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.880
Faris states that she was good friends with&nbsp;
Jennifer Lawrence and was embarrassed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.040
gossip. Faris also writes that Lawrence&nbsp;
was apologetic about the whole thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.680
as she knew it was adding even more&nbsp;
stress onto Faris during a stressful time.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.040
While Jennifer Lawrence has mostly unpleasant&nbsp;
memories of filming Passengers' romance scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.040
it wasn't all bad. In true Jennifer&nbsp;
Lawrence-style, she liked them the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.920
most when they went off the rails, generating&nbsp;
some of the best moments on the film's set.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:43.040
During an interview with Lawrence, USA Today&nbsp;
discovered that one of Passengers' funniest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.320
moments was completely unintentional. In the&nbsp;
movie, Lawrence and Pratt's characters eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:54.000
don space suits, and after they take the helmets&nbsp;
off, they go in for a kiss... but bump into each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.200
other because the suits are so big. That wasn't&nbsp;
supposed to happen. They were supposed to lock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.480
lips passionately, but the unforeseen bulky&nbsp;
nature of the space suits transformed the scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.320
into a comedic bit. Everyone on set liked it so&nbsp;
much that it was left in the film's final cut.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:16.240
This unscripted moment is yet another entry in the&nbsp;
list of movie bloopers that were deemed superior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:22.240
to the intended versions. Coincidentally, another&nbsp;
recent example of such a scene also involves Chris&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:28.800
Pratt — that time he accidentally dropped an&nbsp;
Infinity Stone in Guardians of the Galaxy. Oops.

